Ecosystem: Internet Token Zone Agency 
Domain: itz.agency
Software: itzd
Options:
	itzd config
	itzd login
	itzd api-key key.json
	itzd api <args>
	itzd dns network <name> <value> <ttl> <args>
	itzd wallet network <name> <value> <wallet> <args>
	itzd peers network <opts>
	itzd network <net> transactions
	itzd balances <network>
	itzd daemon <start|stop|pause|refresh|restart>
	itzd dns grpc 

config - would set up the config for the client and link it to the website
       - create keys used for peer to peer
       - tag wallets
       - add metadata
login - will into the itz network
api-key - can be used to create api keys
dns network ... for managing the wallets in our DNS
wallet for creating wallets
peers show local peers, hashed
network view dns transations on a given network
show balances of wallet
daemon run as a service
launch a grpc server

Now imagine this:

We support regular DNS and experimental dns records
itzd can be used to create a distributed dns <-> wallet resolution service
can cache name to wallet resolution lookups
other things I didn't think

